{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile is clearly the strongest signal (acc ~0.65), while image-only with resnet50 is very weak (acc 0.208). However, we have only tested one image encoder (resnet50); ViT-L pretrained on ImageNet is substantially more expressive and may extract meaningful cellular morphology signal. Uncertainty: it is unknown whether the image modality contributes any useful information at all, or whether the poor resnet50 result reflects a fundamental lack of signal in the images. This experiment (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) isolates the effect of a stronger image encoder while keeping the setting minimal (no aggregation, no fusion), directly comparable to config_010. Why this is the best next step: before investing budget in any of the 36 multimodal configurations, we need to know whether the image channel has any predictive value. If ViT-L image is still near-chance, multimodal fusion is unlikely to help and remaining budget should focus on RNA-only refinements (e.g., scvi_n200 multiprofile with different aggregation). If ViT-L image is competitive, it justifies exploring multimodal fusion with the proven scvi_n200 multiprofile backbone. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis (whether to include image at all) at minimal cost."
}

